  "prefLabel": "En 1302.13 Pole",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1302.13 “Pole” means “pole” as defined in RSA 374:34-a, I, namely “any pole, duct, conduit, or right-of-way that is used for wire communications or electricity distribution and is owned in whole or in part by a public utility, including a rural electric cooperative for which a certificate of deregulation is on file with the commission pursuant to RSA 301:57.”\n\nSource. #13497, eff 12-1-22 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 1300)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1300.html"
